{
  "name": "What to Expect During a Bathroom Tub to Shower Conversion",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Converting your old bathtub into a sleek, modern shower is a popular choice, and knowing what to expect can make the process much smoother. Usually, this project kicks off with demolition – saying goodbye to your old tub! Once that's out, your contractor will check what’s behind it. This is a critical step because it reveals if there's any hidden damage, like water rot, or if any adjustments are needed for plumbing and electrical lines. Depending on your design, plumbing might need to be relocated for a new showerhead or valves, and electrical might be adjusted for new lighting or a fan. After any necessary adjustments, proper waterproofing is absolutely essential for the exposed wet area. This isn't something you want to skip or skimp on! It prevents future leaks and protects your home. Finally, it’s all about the finishes – installing new tile or wall panels to create that fresh, new shower space you've been dreaming of. The timeline for this really depends on the complexity; a simple swap might be quicker, but if it’s part of a broader bathroom remodel, it could take weeks to months. Keep in mind that product availability can also extend the schedule, so planning ahead for materials is key. HH Remodeling LLC has open communication channels throughout the process, so you’ll always know what’s happening. Ready to transform your bathroom? Contact HH Remodeling LLC to get started.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
